    "_postman_id": "ebf2104b-0006-4795-b4f2-51ea26b50c1a",
    "name": "Cancellation flow",
    "description": "Demonstrates a patient-initiated appointment cancellation and its effect on billing.\n\n**Cancellation rules**\n\n- **Paid appointment, more than 24 hours before its start:** cancellation triggers a refund.\n    \n- **Paid appointment, 24 hours or less before its start:** the appointment is cancelled without a refund.\n    \n- **Unpaid appointment:** the appointment is cancelled without a refund.\n    \n\n**Prerequisites**\n\n- The Scheduling and Billing services and their required infrastructure are running.\n    \n- The selected environment contains `scheduling_url` and `billing_url`.\n    \n- An active appointment eligible for cancellation exists.\n    \n- For a refund scenario, complete a successful payment and use an appointment scheduled more than 24 hours ahead. Keep Stripe webhook forwarding active.\n    \n\n**Request order**\n\n1. **Get the latest active appointment** — retrieve the appointment and save its ID.\n    \n2. StartFragmentRetrieves the invoice status after patient-initiated cancellation.Uses the same `appointmentId` as **Cancel appointment**. No request body is required.The saved examples demonstrate:Billing and refund processing are asynchronous. If the previous state is still shown, wait briefly and query again.Keep the original `appointmentId` throughout the scenario. Do not rerun **Get the latest active appointment** after cancellation, because it may select another appointment.EndFragment  \n    \n    - `CANCELLED`: an invoice cancelled without a refund.\n        \n    - `REFUNDED`: an invoice after the eligible payment was refunded.\n        \n    - **Cancel appointment** — request cancellation with `cancelInitiator` set to `PATIENT`.\n        \n\nCancellation and billing updates are processed across services. Allow time for event and webhook processing before checking the final invoice state.\n\n**Terminology**  \nIn this project, “draft invoice” and “proforma invoice” refer to the same invoice stage. The API represents this stage with `invoiceStatus: DRAFT`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "57059525"
  },
